1. Message Authentication
Message authentication is the process of verifying that a message:

Comes from the claimed sender.
Has not been modified during transmission.
Is received from an authorized source.
It provides assurance about the origin and integrity of a message.

Why is message authentication needed?

Suppose Alice sends Bob a message containing a bank transaction. An attacker may intercept and modify the amount. Message authentication helps Bob detect unauthorized modification and verify the message source.

Methods of Message Authentication
Message Authentication Code (MAC).
Hash functions.
Digital signatures.
1.1 Message Authentication Code (MAC)
