Transport Mode vs Tunnel Mode
Transport Mode

Protects the IP packet's payload.
Original IP header remains visible.
Commonly used for host-to-host communication.
Tunnel Mode

Protects the entire original IP packet by encapsulating it inside a new IP packet.
